From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:41:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Initialize the dependency lookup before its reason is read

DependencyManager::VerifyExistence() declares a CatalogSet::EntryLookup
and fills it on two paths of three: a schema entry, or any other entry
whose schema was found. When the schema path leads nowhere the lookup
is read with its reason uninitialized, which -Wmaybe-uninitialized
reports, and the DELETED test that follows answers from whatever the
stack held. The lookup starts out as NOT_PRESENT with no result, which
is what a missing schema means for its subject.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
 src/duckdb/src/catalog/dependency_manager.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/catalog/dependency_manager.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/catalog/dependency_manager.cpp
index e3d2db1871..3b8f5adc63 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/catalog/dependency_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/catalog/dependency_manager.cpp
@@ -553,7 +553,7 @@ void DependencyManager::VerifyExistence(CatalogTransaction transaction, Dependen
 
 	// navigate the (possibly nested) schema path to the schema that directly contains the subject
 	auto schema = NavigateSchemaPath(transaction, schema_path);
-	CatalogSet::EntryLookup lookup_result;
+	CatalogSet::EntryLookup lookup_result {nullptr, CatalogSet::EntryLookup::FailureReason::NOT_PRESENT};
 	if (type == CatalogType::SCHEMA_ENTRY) {
 		auto &container = schema ? schema->Cast<DuckSchemaEntry>().GetCatalogSet(CatalogType::SCHEMA_ENTRY)
 		                         : catalog.GetSchemaCatalogSet();
